# cargo's build output. `cargo check` and Zed's own extension build both drop
# it here; it is hundreds of MB of intermediates and never belongs in a commit.
# Kept beside the crate rather than in the repo root .gitignore so the
# extension directory is self-contained — everything cargo needs to know about
# this crate is in this directory.
/target/

# Zed's `install dev extension` compiles the crate and writes the built wasm
# INTO this source directory, then loads it from here — so the file must stay
# on disk for the installed dev extension to keep working, and must stay out
# of git for the same reason /target/ does. Untracked, it also read as a
# dirty tree to `k update`'s clean-tree preflight, blocking every update on a
# machine that had merely installed the extension.
extension.wasm
